# Alpha Deathclaw: "When this creature enters or becomes monstrous, destroy target permanent." Each player has one.
# Bot2's is cast on turn 2 (destroying Bot1's Mox Ruby) and Bot1's on turn 3 (destroying Bot2's Mox Ruby). On turn 4
# Bot2's becomes monstrous (Monstrosity 4, {5}{B}{G}) and its own trigger destroys Bot1's Bayou -- Bot1's Deathclaw
# does not trigger: it is another permanent that became monstrous. On turn 5 Bot1's becomes monstrous and destroys
# Bot2's Sol Ring, without a trigger from Bot2's. On turn 7 Bot1 activates Monstrosity again: the creature is already
# monstrous (CR 701.37b), so it gets no more counters and nothing is destroyed.

[Bot1 Deck]
Bayou
Mox Jet
Mox Emerald
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Sol Ring
Alpha Deathclaw
Island
Island
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
